window.VeilGardeData.files["Playground"] = {"group":"Playground","files":[{"path":"Playground/Package.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,23]],"header":null,"marks":[],"first":1893,"scopes":[],"old":"","new":"// swift-tools-version: 6.4\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n// WHAT: The VeilGarde playground, a package of its own: one program, read top to bottom, that runs\n//       VeilGarde's inference regime on this Mac (the warp lens and its camera-sensor score, capture,\n//       fusion, the specialist stack) and, as the layers land, its training regime, the flywheel\n//       and the watermark. Playground/run.sh builds it (release) and runs it.\n// PIN:  VeilGarde by path, Swift 5 mode like VeilGarde's MLX targets. A package rather than an\n//       Xcode playground: MLX finds mlx.metallib only beside the running binary, and training\n//       wants Release (Braid's playground, for the same reasons).\nimport PackageDescription\n\nlet package = Package(\n    name: \"VeilGardePlayground\",\n    platforms: [.macOS(\"26.0\")],\n    dependencies: [.package(path: \"..\")],\n    targets: [\n        .executableTarget(\n            name: \"VeilGardePlayground\",\n            dependencies: [.product(name: \"VeilGarde\", package: \"VeilGarde\")],\n            swiftSettings: [.swiftLanguageMode(.v5)]\n        ),\n    ]\n)\n"},{"path":"Playground/README.md","status":"added","lang":"markdown","hunks":[[1,0,1,41]],"header":null,"marks":[],"first":1893,"scopes":[],"old":"","new":"# The VeilGarde playground\n\nOne program, read top to bottom, that runs VeilGarde on this Mac and checks itself against Garde:\n\n0. **Metal and the bundle.** MLX's Metal library beside the binary; the shipped bundle verified against its manifest.\n1. **The images.** The two parity crops Garde scored on 2026-10-19, and, when `final_mixed` is under `VEILGARDE_DATASETS` (or the work area's `datasets/`), six iPhone originals and six generated images from it, every k-th by name.\n2. **The warp lens.** One image cut into 32-px tiles, each warped through 16 fixed homographies and back; the centre tile's 19 features by name.\n3. **The camera-sensor score.** The warp tile model alone: P(generated) per tile, the tile vote, and the two cuts that call it (real at or under 0.7169 of the tiles, generated at or over 0.8365), with the call's trust; the weighted warp score at 0.56 ± 0.04. Then the same score on the iPhone and generated sample.\n4. **Capture.** The native Nyquist peak and the screenshot gate.\n5. **Fusion.** The 397-column vector and the fusion head's base P(AI).\n6. **The specialists.** The full detector's stack, the combiner's arithmetic term by term, and the routed result against Garde's goldens.\n7. **Training, in miniature.** A `TrainingRecipe` written in Swift (a toy warp tile model, a warm start on the shipped fusion head, the human head, the combiner), its plan, and the engine's run into a candidate bundle in `Playground/.work/candidates/playground`. The toy warp model trains on the final_mixed sample's tiles, cut by the warp lens; the heads and the combiner train on a seeded sample of the work area's feature store when this Mac has it. Without that sample or that store, seeded synthetic tiles and rows stand in, and the step says so. Its calibration is fitted by hand, since a dozen images are below the engine's floors of 25 and 15 per class, and said as two cuts on the vote, as the engine writes it.\n8. **The flywheel.** The specialist regime alone, in `Playground/.work`: the shipped bundle copied as the live bundle, a regression battery (every image keeps the call the shipped detector gives it, as HARD groups), the frozen warp tile model refused, the human head from step 7 promoted behind its admission gate and the battery, the promote log, and a rollback.\n9. **The watermark.** The first parity crop signed by its own fragility pattern (four ordinal bits a tile, sectioned 4×4), matched against itself, then a half-area crop at a seeded random offset found by the phase search, and a JPEG q75 re-encode; the crop and the re-encode are reported, not asserted.\n10. **Verify.** Every checkpoint; the exit code is 0 only when all hold.\n\n## Run\n\n```sh\nscripts/cli.sh weights import-dinov2   # once: DINOv2's weights into the work area\nPlayground/run.sh                      # builds release, installs mlx.metallib, runs\n```\n\nThe first build compiles Frigate's MLX and takes minutes. From Xcode, open `Playground/Package.swift` and Run; step 0 copies a staged `mlx.metallib` beside Xcode's binary.\n\n## What the checkpoints compare\n\n- The warp lens's result JSON equals Garde's leaf for leaf, `times_sec` and the sensor fields the two cuts changed on purpose aside, and makes Garde's call.\n- The routed result matches Garde's with every label exact and every number within 1e-4, the same sensor fields aside. Under Garde's own Metal library it was byte-identical (37 of 37 images, 2026-10-19, before the two cuts); under Frigate's current library DINOv2's matrix kernels move its outputs by about 1e-5.\n- The combiner computed by hand equals the router's pre-semantic score.\n- The toy warp model, written as XGBoost JSON, reads back through Frigate's evaluator with identical predictions on every tile.\n- The toy calibration contract binds to the toy model's bytes and refuses the shipped model's.\n- The warm start keeps the shipped fusion head's 940 trees byte for byte and adds two.\n- The candidate bundle verifies: every artifact's hash matches its manifest.\n- Promote refuses the frozen warp tile model.\n- The watermarked image matches its own signature at offset (0, 0) with score 1.\n- After the promote and its rollback (or a refused promote), the frozen artifacts' bytes are unchanged and the live bundle is byte for byte what it was.\n\nIt writes nothing outside `Playground/.work` (gitignored), and only from step 7 on. Run the candidate it trains with\n`scripts/cli.sh route <image> --bundle Playground/.work/candidates/playground`, and look at its flywheel with\n`scripts/cli.sh flywheel status --work-area Playground/.work`.\n"},{"path":"Playground/Sources/VeilGardePlayground/Golden.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,37]],"header":{"lines":[1,8],"target":"VeilGardePlayground","what":[6,7],"pin":null,"in":null,"out":null,"style":"swift"},"marks":[],"first":1893,"scopes":[["E","Golden",null,"",13,13,[13,12],37,null,-1,0,"a",[]],["f","leaves",["_","_"],"static",14,14,[14,77],18,null,0,0,"a"],["f","compare",["_","_","tolerance"],"static",20,20,[20,113],36,null,0,0,"a"]],"old":"","new":"//\n//  Golden.swift\n//  VeilGardePlayground\n//  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n//\n//  WHAT: Comparing a result JSON with Garde's: every label exact and every number within a tolerance,\n//        times_sec and the sensor fields the two cuts changed on purpose (ResultJSON.changedSinceGarde) aside.\n//\n\nimport Foundation\nimport VeilGarde\n\nenum Golden {\n    static func leaves(_ value: Any, _ path: String = \"\") -> [(String, Any)] {\n        if let d = value as? [String: Any] { return d.keys.sorted().flatMap { leaves(d[$0]!, path.isEmpty ? $0 : \"\\(path).\\($0)\") } }\n        if let a = value as? [Any] { return a.enumerated().flatMap { leaves($1, \"\\(path)[\\($0)]\") } }\n        return [(path, value)]\n    }\n\n    static func compare(_ a: Data, _ b: Data, tolerance: Double) throws -> (worst: Double, mismatches: [String]) {\n        let kept: ((String, Any)) -> Bool = { !$0.0.hasPrefix(\"times_sec\") && !ResultJSON.changedSinceGarde($0.0) }\n        let x = Dictionary(uniqueKeysWithValues: leaves(try JSONSerialization.jsonObject(with: a)).filter(kept))\n        let y = Dictionary(uniqueKeysWithValues: leaves(try JSONSerialization.jsonObject(with: b)).filter(kept))\n        var worst = 0.0\n        var mismatches = Array(Set(x.keys).symmetricDifference(y.keys)).sorted()\n        for key in Set(x.keys).intersection(y.keys) {\n            if let m = x[key] as? NSNumber, let n = y[key] as? NSNumber, CFGetTypeID(m) != CFBooleanGetTypeID() {\n                let d = abs(m.doubleValue - n.doubleValue)\n                worst = max(worst, d)\n                if d > tolerance { mismatches.append(key) }\n            } else if \"\\(x[key]!)\" != \"\\(y[key]!)\" {\n                mismatches.append(key)\n            }\n        }\n        return (worst, mismatches)\n    }\n}\n"},{"path":"Playground/Sources/VeilGardePlayground/Images.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,55]],"header":{"lines":[1,9],"target":"VeilGardePlayground","what":[6,8],"pin":null,"in":null,"out":null,"style":"swift"},"marks":[],"first":1896,"scopes":[["S","PlaygroundImage",null,"",14,14,[14,23],21,null,-1,0,"a"],["E","Images",null,"",23,23,[23,12],55,null,-1,0,"a",[]],["v","parityCrops",null,"static",34,34,[34,46],38,null,1,0,"a"],["f","sample",["perClass"],"static",41,41,[41,63],54,[40,40],1,0,"a"]],"old":"","new":"//\n//  Images.swift\n//  VeilGardePlayground\n//  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n//\n//  WHAT: The images the playground runs: the two parity crops whose results Garde wrote on\n//        2026-10-19 (the goldens every step checks against), and, when the T9 is mounted, a seeded\n//        sample of iPhone originals and generated images from final_mixed (read only).\n//\n\nimport Foundation\nimport VeilGarde\n\nstruct PlaygroundImage {\n    let name: String\n    let url: URL\n    /// 0 real, 1 generated, nil unknown.\n    let label: Int?\n    /// Garde's route JSON for this image, when it is a parity crop.\n    let gardeRoute: URL?\n}\n\nenum Images {\n    static let repoRoot: URL = {\n        var url = URL(fileURLWithPath: #filePath)\n        while url.lastPathComponent != \"Playground\" { url.deleteLastPathComponent() }\n        return url.deletingLastPathComponent()\n    }()\n\n    static let goldens = repoRoot.appendingPathComponent(\"Tests/VeilGardeInferenceTests/Fixtures/garde\")\n    /// final_mixed under VEILGARDE_DATASETS (else the work area's datasets/), for the optional labelled sample.\n    static let finalMixed = (WorkArea.datasets() ?? URL(fileURLWithPath: \"datasets\", isDirectory: true)).appendingPathComponent(\"final_mixed\")\n\n    static var parityCrops: [PlaygroundImage] {\n        [\"crop_ben\", \"crop_fox\"].map {\n            PlaygroundImage(name: \"\\($0).png\", url: goldens.appendingPathComponent(\"\\($0).png\"), label: nil, gardeRoute: goldens.appendingPathComponent(\"\\($0).route.json\"))\n        }\n    }\n\n    /// Up to `perClass` iPhone originals and generated images, every k-th by name.\n    static func sample(perClass: Int = 6) -> [PlaygroundImage] {\n        var out: [PlaygroundImage] = []\n        for (folder, prefix, label) in [(\"real\", \"iphone_real_\", 0), (\"generated\", \"\", 1)] {\n            let dir = finalMixed.appendingPathComponent(folder)\n            let names = ((try? FileManager.default.contentsOfDirectory(atPath: dir.path)) ?? [])\n                .filter { !$0.hasPrefix(\".\") && $0.hasPrefix(prefix) && [\"jpg\", \"jpeg\", \"png\"].contains(($0 as NSString).pathExtension.lowercased()) }.sorted()\n            guard !names.isEmpty else { continue }\n            let step = max(1, names.count / perClass)\n            for name in names.enumerated().filter({ $0.offset % step == 0 }).prefix(perClass).map(\\.element) {\n                out.append(PlaygroundImage(name: name, url: dir.appendingPathComponent(name), label: label, gardeRoute: nil))\n            }\n        }\n        return out\n    }\n}\n"},{"path":"Playground/Sources/VeilGardePlayground/Scratch.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,34]],"header":{"lines":[1,9],"target":"VeilGardePlayground","what":[6,8],"pin":null,"in":null,"out":null,"style":"swift"},"marks":[],"first":1900,"scopes":[["E","Scratch",null,"",14,14,[14,13],34,null,-1,0,"a",[]],["v","workArea",null,"static",17,17,[17,34],17,null,0,8,"a"],["f","installMetalLibrary",[],"static",20,20,[20,56],33,[19,19],0,0,"a"]],"old":"","new":"//\n//  Scratch.swift\n//  VeilGardePlayground\n//  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n//\n//  WHAT: The playground's own work area (Playground/.work, gitignored) and MLX's Metal library\n//        beside whichever binary runs: run.sh installs it, and a run from Xcode copies the one\n//        Frigate's build-metallib.sh staged.\n//\n\nimport Foundation\nimport VeilGarde\n\nenum Scratch {\n    static let work = Images.repoRoot.appendingPathComponent(\"Playground/.work\", isDirectory: true)\n\n    static var workArea: WorkArea { WorkArea(root: work) }\n\n    /// Copies a staged mlx.metallib beside this binary when none is there; returns its source.\n    static func installMetalLibrary() throws -> String? {\n        guard let binary = Bundle.main.executableURL else { return nil }\n        let target = binary.deletingLastPathComponent().appendingPathComponent(\"mlx.metallib\")\n        if FileManager.default.fileExists(atPath: target.path) { return nil }\n        let candidates = [\n            Images.repoRoot.appendingPathComponent(\".build/out/Products/Release/mlx.metallib\"),\n            Images.repoRoot.appendingPathComponent(\".build/out/Products/Debug/mlx.metallib\"),\n        ]\n        guard let source = candidates.first(where: { FileManager.default.fileExists(atPath: $0.path) }) else {\n            throw VeilGardeFailure.missing(\"no mlx.metallib beside \\(binary.path)\", hint: \"run Playground/run.sh, which installs it\")\n        }\n        try FileManager.default.copyItem(at: source, to: target)\n        return source.path\n    }\n}\n"},{"path":"Playground/Sources/VeilGardePlayground/Show.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,46]],"header":{"lines":[1,8],"target":"VeilGardePlayground","what":[6,7],"pin":null,"in":null,"out":null,"style":"swift"},"marks":[],"first":1903,"scopes":[["E","Show",null,"",13,13,[13,10],34,null,-1,0,"a",[]],["f","step",["_","_","_"],"static",14,14,[14,63],16,null,0,0,"a"],["f","line",["_"],"static",18,18,[18,37],18,null,0,8,"a"],["f","map",["_"],"static",21,21,[21,42],31,[20,20],0,0,"a"],["f","f",["_","_"],"static",33,33,[33,59],33,null,0,8,"a"],["C","Checkpoints",null,"final",37,37,[37,24],46,[36,36],-1,0,"a"],["f","record",["_","_"],"",40,40,[40,44],43,null,5,0,"a"],["v","passed",null,"",45,45,[45,21],45,null,5,8,"a"]],"old":"","new":"//\n//  Show.swift\n//  VeilGardePlayground\n//  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n//\n//  WHAT: How the playground prints: numbered step headers, a compact P(generated) map, and the\n//        checkpoints it collects for the last step.\n//\n\nimport Foundation\nimport VeilGarde\n\nenum Show {\n    static func step(_ n: Int, _ name: String, _ text: String) {\n        print(\"\\(String(n).padding(toLength: 3, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0))\\(name.padding(toLength: 12, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0))\\(text)\")\n    }\n\n    static func line(_ text: String) { print(\"               \" + text) }\n\n    /// The sensor map as two-digit percentages, every second row and column for a 16×16 grid.\n    static func map(_ r: InferenceResult) {\n        let stride = r.gridCols > 12 ? 2 : 1\n        for i in Swift.stride(from: 0, to: r.gridRows, by: stride) {\n            var row = \"\"\n            for j in Swift.stride(from: 0, to: r.gridCols, by: stride) {\n                let p = r.patches[i * r.gridCols + j].pGenerated\n                row += String(format: \"%3.0f\", p * 100)\n            }\n            line(row)\n        }\n    }\n\n    static func f(_ x: Float, _ digits: Int = 4) -> String { String(format: \"%.\\(digits)f\", x) }\n}\n\n/// Every checkpoint the playground makes, for the verify step and the exit code.\nfinal class Checkpoints {\n    private(set) var all: [(String, Bool)] = []\n\n    func record(_ name: String, _ ok: Bool) {\n        all.append((name, ok))\n        Show.line(\"\\(ok ? \"✓\" : \"✗\") \\(name)\")\n    }\n\n    var passed: Bool { all.allSatisfy(\\.1) }\n}\n"},{"path":"Playground/Sources/VeilGardePlayground/Toy.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,104]],"header":{"lines":[1,11],"target":"VeilGardePlayground","what":[6,9],"pin":[10,10],"in":null,"out":null,"style":"swift"},"marks":[],"first":1911,"scopes":[["E","Toy",null,"",16,16,[16,9],104,null,-1,0,"a",[]],["f","writeDataset",["_"],"static",25,25,[25,75],59,[23,24],0,0,"a"],["f","writeStore",[],"static",62,62,[62,46],103,[61,61],0,0,"a"],["f","gauss",[],"",82,82,[82,30],82,null,2,12,"a"]],"old":"","new":"//\n//  Toy.swift\n//  VeilGardePlayground\n//  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n//\n//  WHAT: The training regime in miniature, on real code paths: a dataset of the final_mixed\n//        sample (its tiles cut by the warp lens into Playground/.work), and a small store, a\n//        seeded sample of the work area's feature store when this Mac has it. Without the T9 or\n//        that store, seeded synthetic tiles and rows take their place, and the output says so.\n//  PIN:  Writes only Playground/.work; reads final_mixed and the work area's store, never writes them.\n//\n\nimport Foundation\nimport VeilGarde\n\nenum Toy {\n    static let dataset = Scratch.work.appendingPathComponent(\"toy/dataset.jsonl\")\n    static let store = Scratch.work.appendingPathComponent(\"store/shards\", isDirectory: true)\n    /// The work area's feature store (VEILGARDE_SEED_STORE names another), read, never written.\n    static let seedStore = URL(fileURLWithPath: ProcessInfo.processInfo.environment[\"VEILGARDE_SEED_STORE\"]\n        ?? WorkArea.resolve()?.shards.path ?? \"store/shards\", isDirectory: true)\n\n    /// The toy dataset: the labeled sample, two of each class held out for validation. Returns\n    /// what it is made of.\n    static func writeDataset(_ sample: [PlaygroundImage]) throws -> String {\n        try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: dataset.deletingLastPathComponent())\n        let labeled = sample.filter { $0.label != nil }\n        if labeled.count >= 8 {\n            var records: [ImageRecord] = []\n            for label in [0, 1] {\n                for (k, image) in labeled.filter({ $0.label == label }).enumerated() {\n                    records.append(ImageRecord(path: image.url.path, label: label, stem: (image.name as NSString).deletingPathExtension,\n                                               split: k < 2 ? .val : .train))\n                }\n            }\n            try ImageManifest(records: records, root: dataset.deletingLastPathComponent()).write(to: dataset)\n            return \"\\(records.count) final_mixed images (\\(records.filter { $0.split == .train }.count) train, \\(records.filter { $0.split == .val }.count) validation)\"\n        }\n        // No T9: 120 synthetic images whose tiles are written straight into the cache.\n        var rng = SplitMix64(seed: 5)\n        let records = (0..<120).map { ImageRecord(path: \"synthetic/\\($0).png\", label: $0 % 2, stem: String(format: \"synthetic_%03d\", $0), split: $0 % 5 == 0 ? .val : .train) }\n        let manifest = ImageManifest(records: records, root: dataset.deletingLastPathComponent())\n        try manifest.write(to: dataset)\n        var images: [TileImage] = [], features: [Float] = [], texture: [Float] = []\n        for r in records {\n            images.append(TileImage(stem: r.stem, path: r.path, label: r.label, split: r.split!, pool: nil, tag: nil, rows: 4, cols: 4, start: texture.count, width: 128, height: 128))\n            for _ in 0..<16 {\n                var row = (0..<WarpFeatures.count).map { _ in Float(rng.unit()) }\n                row[0] = Float(rng.unit()) * 0.6 + (r.label == 1 ? 0.3 : 0)\n                features += row\n                texture.append(Float(0.2 + rng.unit()))\n            }\n        }\n        let cache = Scratch.work.appendingPathComponent(\"store/tiles/dataset\", isDirectory: true)\n        try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: cache)\n        try FileManager.default.createDirectory(at: cache, withIntermediateDirectories: true)\n        try TileShard(name: \"tiles_0000\", images: images, features: features, texture: texture).write(to: cache)\n        return \"120 synthetic images (the T9 is not mounted; their tiles are seeded, not measured)\"\n    }\n\n    /// The toy store: per (category, label) group a seeded handful of the store's rows, or synthetic rows.\n    static func writeStore() throws -> String {\n        try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: store)\n        try FileManager.default.createDirectory(at: store, withIntermediateDirectories: true)\n        let quota: [String: Int] = [\"human/1\": 120, \"art/1\": 120, \"art/0\": 80, \"photo/0\": 160, \"wildlife/0\": 80, \"human/0\": 80, \"video/1\": 60, \"cgi/1\": 40, \"cgi/0\": 40]\n        if FileManager.default.fileExists(atPath: seedStore.path) {\n            let all = try FeatureStore(directory: seedStore).select(columns: Set(FeatureColumn.allCases)) { !$0.nsfw }\n            var picked: [Int] = []\n            var groups: [String: [Int]] = [:]\n            for i in 0..<all.count { groups[\"\\(all.rows[i].category)/\\(all.rows[i].label)\", default: []].append(i) }\n            for (key, members) in groups.sorted(by: { $0.key < $1.key }) {\n                let ordered = members.sorted { StableSplit.unit(all.rows[$0].id, salt: \"playground\") < StableSplit.unit(all.rows[$1].id, salt: \"playground\") }\n                let golden = ordered.filter { all.rows[$0].golden }\n                picked += ordered.filter { !all.rows[$0].golden }.prefix(quota[key] ?? 0) + golden.prefix(key.hasSuffix(\"/0\") ? 40 : 0)\n            }\n            picked.sort()\n            let sample = all.subset(picked)\n            try FeatureShard(name: \"seed_sample\", rows: sample.rows, columns: sample.columns).write(to: store)\n            return \"\\(sample.count) rows of the work area's feature store (\\(sample.rows.filter(\\.golden).count) golden anchors), copied read-only\"\n        }\n        var rng = SplitMix64(seed: 9)\n        func gauss() -> Float { Float((-2 * log(max(1e-12, rng.unit()))).squareRoot() * cos(2 * .pi * rng.unit())) }\n        var rows: [FeatureRow] = []\n        var columns: [FeatureColumn: [Float]] = Dictionary(uniqueKeysWithValues: FeatureColumn.allCases.map { ($0, [Float]()) })\n        let sources = [\"civitai\", \"commons_native\", \"inat\", \"hf_faces\", \"wikimedia\"]\n        for (key, n) in quota.sorted(by: { $0.key < $1.key }) {\n            let parts = key.split(separator: \"/\"), category = String(parts[0]), label = Int(parts[1])!\n            for k in 0..<n {\n                rows.append(FeatureRow(id: ContentHash.sha1Hex(Data(\"\\(key)-\\(k)\".utf8)), path: \"/synthetic/\\(key)/\\(k)\", label: label, category: category,\n                                       source: sources[k % sources.count], golden: label == 0 && k % 9 == 0))\n                var norm = (0..<384).map { _ in gauss() }\n                if label == 1 { for j in 0..<16 { norm[j + (category == \"human\" ? 0 : 20)] += 1.5 } }\n                columns[.dinoNorm]! += norm\n                columns[.dinoFusion]! += (0..<384).map { j in gauss() + (label == 1 && j < 8 ? 1 : 0) }\n                columns[.cap]! += [Float(rng.unit() * 40), 1, 0, 2000, 5, 0.5, 0.5, 0.5, 0]\n                columns[.warp]!.append(Float(0.4 + (label == 1 ? 0.2 : 0) + 0.1 * Double(gauss())))\n                columns[.sharp]! += [10, 10, 1]\n                columns[.noiseprint]!.append(Float(label == 0 ? 0.6 : 0.3))\n            }\n        }\n        try FeatureShard(name: \"synthetic\", rows: rows, columns: columns).write(to: store)\n        return \"\\(rows.count) synthetic rows (no feature store on this Mac)\"\n    }\n}\n"},{"path":"Playground/Sources/VeilGardePlayground/main.swift","status":"added","lang":"swift","hunks":[[1,0,1,300]],"header":{"lines":[1,23],"target":"VeilGardePlayground","what":[6,14],"pin":[19,22],"in":[15,16],"out":[17,18],"style":"swift"},"marks":[],"first":1915,"scopes":[["f","run",[],"",31,31,[31,18],292,null,-1,0,"a"]],"old":"","new":"//\n//  main.swift\n//  VeilGardePlayground\n//  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n//\n//  WHAT: VeilGarde end to end, top to bottom. The inference regime first, one core part at a time: the\n//        warp lens on one image (its tiles and their 19 features), the base warp model alone and\n//        the camera-sensor score it yields (did a real camera make this?), the capture signature,\n//        the fusion head, then the stacked specialists and the full verdict, the combiner's\n//        arithmetic printed term by term. Then the training regime in miniature (step 7: a\n//        recipe, its plan, the engine, a candidate bundle), the flywheel loop (step 8: a live\n//        bundle, a battery, a promote and its rollback) and the watermark (step 9: a signature\n//        from the same residual, matched by a crop and a re-encode). Every step checks itself against\n//        Garde's goldens where one exists.\n//  IN:   The weights in the work area or VEILGARDE_WEIGHTS; final_mixed under VEILGARDE_DATASETS\n//        for the iPhone sample (optional). Run by Playground/run.sh.\n//  OUT:  One numbered block per step; Playground/.work for the training steps. Exit 0 only when\n//        every checkpoint holds.\n//  PIN:  One MLX workload at a time; everything runs on this thread. Checkpoints compare against\n//        Garde: the warp lens leaf for leaf, the routed result with labels exact and numbers within\n//        1e-4 (Frigate's Metal kernels move DINOv2 by about 1e-5), both but for the sensor fields the\n//        two cuts changed on purpose (ResultJSON.changedSinceGarde), whose call is Garde's.\n//\n\nimport Foundation\nimport VeilGarde\n\nsetvbuf(stdout, nil, _IOLBF, 0)\nlet checks = Checkpoints()\n\nfunc run() throws {\n    // 0. MLX's Metal library beside this binary, before anything touches MLX.\n    if let source = try Scratch.installMetalLibrary() { Show.step(0, \"metal\", \"mlx.metallib copied beside this binary from \\(source)\") }\n    ShippedBundle.registerWeightFolders()\n    let bundle = try ShippedBundle.verified()\n    Show.step(0, \"bundle\", \"the shipped bundle: \\(bundle.manifest.artifacts.count) artifacts verified against manifest.json\")\n\n    // 1. The images.\n    let crops = Images.parityCrops\n    let sample = Images.sample()\n    Show.step(1, \"images\", \"\\(crops.count) parity crops with Garde's goldens\" + (sample.isEmpty ? \"; the T9 is not mounted, no iPhone sample\" : \"; \\(sample.count) from final_mixed (\\(sample.filter { $0.label == 0 }.count) iPhone originals, \\(sample.filter { $0.label == 1 }.count) generated)\"))\n\n    // 2. The warp lens on one image: tiles, the residual, the 19 features of one tile.\n    let first = crops[0]\n    let cg = try ImageDecoding.cgImage(contentsOf: first.url)\n    let (tiles, geometry) = try WarpLens.tileFeatures(cgImage: cg)\n    Show.step(2, \"lens\", \"\\(first.name): \\(cg.width)×\\(cg.height), scored \\(geometry.scoringWidth)×\\(geometry.scoringHeight) as \\(tiles.tileRows)×\\(tiles.tileCols) tiles of 32 px\")\n    Show.line(\"each tile warped through 16 fixed homographies at strengths 0.025 and 0.05 and back; the round-trip residual, high-passed, is measured\")\n    let centre = (tiles.tileRows / 2) * tiles.tileCols + tiles.tileCols / 2\n    let row = tiles.row(centre)\n    Show.line(\"the centre tile's 19 features:\")\n    for (k, name) in WarpFeatures.names.enumerated() { Show.line(\"  \" + name.padding(toLength: 12, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0) + String(format: \"%10.5f\", row[row.startIndex + k])) }\n    let meanFR = (0..<tiles.count).map { tiles.row($0).first! }.reduce(0, +) / Float(tiles.count)\n    Show.line(\"mean fragility rate over the image: \\(Show.f(meanFR))\")\n\n    // 3. The base warp model alone, and the camera-sensor score.\n    let config = InferenceConfig()\n    let warp = try WarpInference.run(cgImage: cg, config: config)\n    Show.step(3, \"sensor\", \"the warp tile model (200 trees, depth 8, 19 features) scores every tile: P(generated) per tile, every second shown\")\n    Show.map(warp)\n    let n = warp.gridRows * warp.gridCols\n    let raw = warp.sensorRawProbability ?? 0\n    let contract = warp.sensorCalibration!\n    let cuts = contract.cuts!\n    Show.line(\"tile vote: \\(Int((raw * Float(n)).rounded())) of \\(n) tiles above 0.5 → the camera-sensor score \\(Show.f(raw))\")\n    Show.line(\"two cuts on the vote: real at or under \\(Show.f(Float(cuts.realAtOrBelow))), generated at or over \\(Show.f(Float(cuts.generatedAtOrAbove))), inconclusive between\")\n    Show.line(\"→ \\(warp.sensorPrediction ?? \"?\"), trust \\(Trust.sensorVote(warp, route: \"camera\"))\")\n    Show.line(\"weighted warp score \\(Show.f(warp.weightedScore)) against 0.56 ± 0.04 → \\(warp.weightedPrediction)\")\n    let (warpWorst, warpMismatches) = try Golden.compare(try ResultJSON.encode(warp, times: [], device: \"gpu\"),\n                                                         try Data(contentsOf: Images.goldens.appendingPathComponent(\"crop_ben.score.json\")), tolerance: 0)\n    checks.record(\"the warp lens's JSON equals Garde's leaf for leaf but for the sensor fields the cuts changed, with Garde's call (\\(first.name))\",\n                  warpMismatches.isEmpty && warpWorst == 0 && warp.sensorProbability == raw)\n    if !sample.isEmpty {\n        Show.line(\"\")\n        Show.line(\"the camera-sensor score on the final_mixed sample (physics alone, no semantics):\")\n        Show.line(\"image\".padding(toLength: 28, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0) + \"truth      sensor p  call          trust  capture\")\n        for image in sample {\n            let r = try WarpInference.run(cgImage: try ImageDecoding.cgImage(contentsOf: image.url), config: config)\n            let truth = image.label == 0 ? \"camera\" : \"generated\"\n            Show.line(image.name.padding(toLength: 28, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0) + truth.padding(toLength: 11, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0)\n                      + Show.f(r.sensorProbability ?? 0) + \"    \" + (r.sensorPrediction ?? \"?\").padding(toLength: 14, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0)\n                      + Trust.sensorVote(r, route: \"camera\").padding(toLength: 7, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0)\n                      + (r.captureSignature.map { $0.present ? \"present\" : ($0.valid ? \"absent\" : \"invalid\") } ?? \"?\"))\n            LensRuntime.releaseMemory()\n        }\n        Show.line(\"trust is high only for a binary call on a native camera route with a present capture signature that the weighted verdict agrees with\")\n        Show.line(\"(trust law v1): the sensor score is a camera detector, not a generator detector; the fusion and the specialists catch generators\")\n    }\n\n    // 4. The capture signature and the screenshot gate.\n    let capture = CaptureLens.features(cg)\n    let gate = ScreenshotLens.gate(cg)\n    Show.step(4, \"capture\", \"native Nyquist peak \\(Show.f(capture.peak, 1)) (present at ≥ 30 when the short side ≥ 512): \\(capture.signature.present ? \"a real sensor's mosaic is present\" : \"absent\")\")\n    Show.line(\"screenshot gate: grad_zero \\(Show.f(gate.gradZero, 3)), flat_strict \\(Show.f(gate.flatStrict, 3)), top_color \\(Show.f(gate.topColor, 3)) → \\(gate.isScreenshot ? \"screenshot\" : \"not a screenshot\")\")\n\n    // 5. The fusion head: the camera base expert.\n    let embedding = try SemanticLens.fusionEmbedding(cg)\n    let s = warp.sharpness!\n    let vector = [warp.weightedScore] + embedding + capture.asVector + [s.salientSharp, s.globalSharp, s.sharpRatio]\n    let fusionHead = try TreeModelCache.shared.model(bundle.url(.fusionHead)!)\n    let baseP = fusionHead.predict(vector)\n    Show.step(5, \"fusion\", \"warp weighted \\(Show.f(warp.weightedScore)) ⊕ DINOv2 CLS (384) ⊕ capture (9) ⊕ sharpness (3) = \\(vector.count) columns\")\n    Show.line(\"→ the fusion head (940 trees: the frozen reference's 900 plus 40 warm-start trees) → base P(AI) \\(Show.f(baseP)) at 0.5 ± 0.04\")\n\n    // 6. The stacked specialists and the full verdict.\n    let routed = try Detector.shared.detect(cgImage: cg, config: config)\n    let r = routed.result\n    Show.step(6, \"specialists\", \"domain \\(routed.domain.rawValue); the stack compounds on the base expert:\")\n    for c in r.specialists ?? [] { Show.line(\"  \" + c.name.padding(toLength: 16, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0) + \"P(AI) \\(Show.f(c.pAI))  \\(c.verdict.padding(toLength: 12, withPad: \" \", startingAt: 0)) weight \\(Show.f(c.weight, 2))\") }\n    if let comb = HeadRegistry.shared.combiner(in: config.bundle), !(r.captureSignature?.present ?? false) {\n        let norm = try SemanticLens.normalizedEmbedding(cg)\n        let heads = HeadKind.combinerOrder.map { HeadRegistry.shared.head($0, in: config.bundle)!.pAI(norm) }\n        let np = NoiseprintLens.score(cg)\n        let ls = comb.headLogits(heads, pairAI: nil)\n        var z = comb.w0 + comb.wBase * comb.lg(baseP, comb.capBase)\n        Show.line(\"the combiner, term by term (capture absent, so it runs):\")\n        Show.line(String(format: \"  w0 %.4f + w_base %.4f · lg(base %.4f) %.4f\", comb.w0, comb.wBase, baseP, comb.lg(baseP, comb.capBase)))\n        for (k, kind) in HeadKind.combinerOrder.enumerated() {\n            z += comb.wGen[k] * max(0, ls[k])\n            Show.line(String(format: \"  + w_gen[%@] %.4f · max(0, lg %.4f)\", kind.rawValue, comb.wGen[k], ls[k]))\n        }\n        if baseP < comb.gateCeiling {\n            let rescue = comb.wRescue * max(0, -(ls.max() ?? -comb.capHead))\n            let camera = (comb.wNp ?? 0) * max(0, comb.lg(np ?? 0.5, comb.capHead))\n            z -= rescue + camera\n            Show.line(String(format: \"  − rescue %.4f − noiseprint %.4f   (base below the 0.75 gate)\", rescue, camera))\n        } else {\n            Show.line(String(format: \"  base %.4f ≥ the 0.75 gate: no rescue, no noiseprint term\", baseP))\n        }\n        let pooled = 1 / (1 + exp(-z))\n        Show.line(String(format: \"  z = %.4f → pooled P(AI) %.4f\", z, pooled))\n        checks.record(\"the hand-computed pool equals the router's pre-semantic score\", abs(pooled - (r.routeDiagnostics?.preSemanticP ?? -1)) < 1e-6)\n    }\n    Show.line(\"verdict: weighted \\(Show.f(r.weightedScore)) \\(r.weightedPrediction); majority (camera-sensor) \\(Show.f(r.majorityScore)) \\(r.majorityPrediction), trust \\(Trust.physicsVote(r))\")\n    for crop in crops {\n        let routedCrop = try Detector.shared.detect(cgImage: try ImageDecoding.cgImage(contentsOf: crop.url), config: config)\n        let ours = try ResultJSON.encode(routedCrop.result, times: [], device: \"route\", route: routedCrop.domain.rawValue)\n        let (worst, mismatches) = try Golden.compare(ours, try Data(contentsOf: crop.gardeRoute!), tolerance: 1e-4)\n        checks.record(\"the routed result matches Garde's for \\(crop.name) but for the sensor fields the cuts changed: labels exact, numbers within 1e-4 (max |Δ| \\(String(format: \"%.2g\", worst)))\", mismatches.isEmpty)\n    }\n\n    // 7. The training regime in miniature: the recipe DSL, the plan, the engine, a candidate bundle.\n    Show.step(7, \"train\", \"the training regime in miniature, on the code paths `veilgarde train` runs\")\n    let made = try Toy.writeDataset(sample)\n    let rows = try Toy.writeStore()\n    Show.line(\"dataset: \\(made)\")\n    Show.line(\"store:   \\(rows)\")\n    let recipe = TrainingRecipe(id: \"playground\") {\n        WarpTileModel(dataset: Toy.dataset).trees(20).depth(4)       // the toy warp tile model\n        FusionHead().warmStart(add: 2, eta: 0.03)                    // the flywheel's only base move\n        DinoHead(.human)                                             // one atlas head, the shipped recipe\n        Combiner()                                                   // pooled over the candidate's heads\n    }\n    Show.line(\"the recipe, as Swift:  WarpTileModel(…).trees(20).depth(4) · FusionHead().warmStart(add: 2) · DinoHead(.human) · Combiner()\")\n    let engine = TrainingEngine(area: Scratch.workArea, parent: ShippedBundle.directory, store: Toy.store) { event in\n        if let line = event.line { Show.line(\"  · \" + line) }\n    }\n    engine.replace = true\n    let plan = try engine.plan(recipe)\n    Show.line(\"the plan (no MLX, no writes):\")\n    for line in plan.summary.split(separator: \"\\n\") { Show.line(\"  \" + line) }\n    let outcome = try engine.train(recipe)\n    var candidate = outcome.candidate\n    Show.line(\"these are toy fits (a dozen images, a few hundred rows), so their numbers mean little: a toy separates its own images\")\n    Show.line(\"perfectly and a weight can run away; `veilgarde train …` runs the same code on final_mixed and the whole store\")\n\n    // The toy warp model is an XGBoost JSON Frigate's evaluator reads unchanged.\n    let toyURL = candidate.url(.warpTile)!\n    let toy = try GBDTModel.load(toyURL)\n    let frigate = try TreeModelCache.shared.model(toyURL)          // Frigate's XGBoostTreeModel\n    let shards = try TileCache(directory: Scratch.work.appendingPathComponent(\"store/tiles/dataset\")).load()\n    let toyTiles = TileSet.gather(shards, partitions: [.train, .val])\n    let rowsF = (0..<toyTiles.tileCount).map { toyTiles.data.row($0) }\n    checks.record(\"the toy warp model (\\(toy.trees.count) trees) reads back through Frigate's evaluator with identical predictions on \\(rowsF.count) tiles\",\n                  rowsF.allSatisfy { frigate.predict($0) == toy.predict($0) })\n\n    // Its calibration, by hand: too few images for the engine's floors (25 and 15 per class).\n    let scores = WarpTrainer.imageScores(toy, toyTiles)\n    let toyPlatt = Platt.fit(labels: toyTiles.images.map(\\.label), probabilities: scores.majority.map(Double.init))\n    let calibrated = Platt.apply(scores.majority.map(Double.init), toyPlatt)\n    let choice = try OperatingThreshold.choose(labels: toyTiles.images.map(\\.label), probabilities: calibrated, maxRealFPR: 0.25)\n    let toySHA = candidate.manifest.artifact(.warpMajoritySensor)!.sha256\n    let fitted = try SensorCalibrationContract(sensorVariant: \"warp19\", sensorModelSHA256: toySHA, transform: .platt, plattPayload: toyPlatt,\n                                               decisionThreshold: Float(choice.threshold), uncertainBand: 0.04)\n    let file = SensorCalibrationFile.twoCuts(from: fitted)!          // where the fitted Platt changes its call\n    let data = try JSONCoding.prettyEncoder().encode(file)\n    try candidate.put(data, as: \"calibration/warp_sensor_calibration.json\", role: .sensorCalibration)\n    Show.line(String(format: \"Platt by hand on %d images' tile votes: σ(%.3f · logit(f) %+.3f), threshold %.3f (recall %.2f at real FPR ≤ 0.25)\",\n                     toyTiles.images.count, toyPlatt.coef, toyPlatt.intercept, choice.threshold, choice.generatedRecall))\n    let (lo, hi) = (file.cuts!.realAtOrBelow, file.cuts!.generatedAtOrAbove)   // a cut outside [0, 1] never fires\n    Show.line(\"said as two cuts on the vote, as the engine writes it: \" + (lo < 0 ? \"never real\" : String(format: \"real at or under %.4f\", lo)) + \", \"\n              + (hi > 1 ? \"never generated\" : String(format: \"generated at or over %.4f\", hi)))\n    let bound = (try? SensorCalibrationContract.decode(data, expectedModelSHA256: toySHA, expectedSensorVariant: \"warp19\")) != nil\n    let unbound = (try? SensorCalibrationContract.decode(data, expectedModelSHA256: bundle.sha256(.warpTile)!, expectedSensorVariant: \"warp19\")) == nil\n    checks.record(\"the toy calibration contract binds to the toy model's bytes and refuses the shipped model's\", bound && unbound)\n\n    // The warm start: the shipped fusion head's 940 trees, untouched, and two more.\n    let shippedHead = try GBDTModel.load(bundle.url(.fusionHead)!)\n    let warm = try GBDTModel.load(candidate.url(.fusionHead)!)\n    let untouched = zip(shippedHead.trees, warm.trees).allSatisfy { $0.raw == $1.raw }\n    checks.record(\"the warm start keeps the shipped fusion head's \\(shippedHead.trees.count) trees byte for byte and adds \\(warm.trees.count - shippedHead.trees.count)\",\n                  untouched && warm.trees.count == shippedHead.trees.count + 2)\n\n    // The trained human head beside the shipped one, on the parity crops.\n    let human = try LinearHead.load(candidate.url(.head, head: .human)!)\n    let shippedHuman = HeadRegistry.shared.head(.human, in: config.bundle)!\n    for crop in crops {\n        let norm = try SemanticLens.normalizedEmbedding(try ImageDecoding.cgImage(contentsOf: crop.url))\n        Show.line(\"\\(crop.name): human head P(AI) \\(Show.f(human.pAI(norm))) trained here, \\(Show.f(shippedHuman.pAI(norm))) shipped\")\n    }\n    var verified = true\n    do { try candidate.verify() } catch { verified = false }\n    checks.record(\"the candidate bundle verifies (\\(candidate.manifest.artifacts.count) artifacts, every hash): \\(candidate.root.path)\", verified)\n    Show.line(\"run it:  scripts/cli.sh route Tests/VeilGardeInferenceTests/Fixtures/garde/crop_ben.png --bundle Playground/.work/candidates/playground\")\n\n    // 8. The flywheel: the specialist regime alone, on Playground/.work.\n    Show.step(8, \"flywheel\", \"the specialist regime alone: a live bundle, a battery, a promote and its rollback, all in Playground/.work\")\n    let fly = FlywheelArea(Scratch.workArea)\n    try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: fly.live)\n    try? FileManager.default.removeItem(at: fly.battery)\n    // A regression battery: every image keeps the call the shipped detector gives it today.\n    let shippedVerdicts = DetectorVerdicts(bundle: .shipped)\n    var keepsReal: [String] = [], keepsGenerated: [String] = []\n    for image in crops + sample {\n        let v = try shippedVerdicts.verdict(for: image.url)\n        if v.weighted == \"real\" { keepsReal.append(image.url.path) } else if v.weighted == \"generated\" { keepsGenerated.append(image.url.path) }\n    }\n    let spec = BatterySpec(groups: [\n        .init(name: \"keeps_real\", mode: .hard, want: \"real\", paths: keepsReal),\n        .init(name: \"keeps_generated\", mode: .hard, want: \"generated\", paths: keepsGenerated),\n    ])\n    let floors = [\"keeps_real\": BatteryGroupResult(acc: 1, n: keepsReal.count, expectedN: nil, inputComplete: nil, semAcc: nil, mode: .hard, want: \"real\"),\n                  \"keeps_generated\": BatteryGroupResult(acc: 1, n: keepsGenerated.count, expectedN: nil, inputComplete: nil, semAcc: nil, mode: .hard, want: \"generated\")]\n    try fly.initialize(from: try ShippedBundle.verified(), spec: try JSONEncoder().encode(spec), baseline: try JSONEncoder().encode(floors),\n                       note: \"the playground's live bundle\")\n    Show.line(\"live: the shipped bundle copied to \\(fly.live.path)\")\n    Show.line(\"battery: \\(keepsReal.count) images that must stay real and \\(keepsGenerated.count) that must stay generated (HARD groups)\")\n    let liveBefore = try fly.liveHashes()\n    let frozenBefore = try fly.liveBundle().manifest.artifacts.filter(\\.frozen).map(\\.sha256)\n    let battery: Promoter.Battery = { gate, root in\n        let report = try BatteryRunner.run(spec: try BatterySpec.load(fly.batterySpec), specURL: fly.batterySpec, gate: gate,\n                                           baselineURL: fly.batteryBaseline, verdicts: DetectorVerdicts(bundle: try DetectorBundle.load(root)))\n        for line in report.table.split(separator: \"\\n\") { Show.line(\"  \" + line) }\n        return report\n    }\n    let promoter = Promoter(area: fly, battery: battery) { Show.line(\"  · \" + $0) }\n    do {\n        _ = try FlywheelSlot(parsing: \"warp-tile\")\n        checks.record(\"promote refuses the frozen warp tile model\", false)\n    } catch {\n        checks.record(\"promote refuses the frozen warp tile model (\\(error))\", true)\n    }\n    Show.line(\"promote the human head step 7 trained, behind admission and the full battery:\")\n    do {\n        let record = try promoter.promote(.head(.human), from: candidate.root, store: FeatureStore(directory: fly.store))\n        Show.line(\"promoted: \\(record.fromSHA256?.prefix(12) ?? \"?\") → \\(record.toSHA256?.prefix(12) ?? \"?\"); now roll it back\")\n        try promoter.rollback(to: record.snapshot!)\n    } catch {\n        Show.line(\"not promoted: \\(error); live was left as it was\")\n    }\n    for line in try String(contentsOf: fly.promoteLog, encoding: .utf8).split(separator: \"\\n\") {\n        if let row = try? JSONCoding.decoder().decode(PromotionRecord.self, from: Data(line.utf8)) { Show.line(\"  log: \\(row.kind.rawValue) \\(row.slot)\" + (row.battery.map { \" (battery \\($0))\" } ?? \"\")) }\n    }\n    let frozenAfter = try fly.liveBundle().manifest.artifacts.filter(\\.frozen).map(\\.sha256)\n    checks.record(\"the frozen artifacts' bytes never moved (\\(frozenBefore.count) of them)\", frozenAfter == frozenBefore)\n    checks.record(\"live is byte for byte what it was before the promote\", try fly.liveHashes() == liveBefore)\n    Show.line(\"look at it:  scripts/cli.sh flywheel status --work-area Playground/.work\")\n\n    // 9. The watermark: the same residual, read as a signature.\n    let markImage = try ImageDecoding.cgImage(contentsOf: crops[0].url)\n    let signature = try Watermark.sign(markImage)\n    Show.step(9, \"watermark\", \"\\(crops[0].name) signed by its fragility pattern: \\(signature.rows)×\\(signature.cols) tiles, \\(signature.codes.count) sections of 4×4, \\(signature.measuredBits) bits\")\n    Show.line(\"each tile's 4 bits: is its fragility rate above its east, south, south-east and north-east neighbours'? (ordinal, so gain-proof)\")\n    Show.line(\"signature: \\(signature.compact.prefix(64))… (\\(signature.binary.count) bytes, cid \\(signature.cid.prefix(16)))\")\n    let me = try Watermark.match(markImage, against: signature, options: MatchOptions(phases: [0]))\n    checks.record(\"the image matches its own signature at offset (0, 0) with score \\(Show.f(Float(me.score), 3))\", me.matched && me.score == 1 && me.offsetX == 0 && me.offsetY == 0)\n    var rng = SplitMix64(seed: 19)\n    let side = Int(Double(markImage.width) * 0.5.squareRoot())\n    let cx = rng.index(markImage.width - side), cy = rng.index(markImage.height - side)\n    if let crop = ImageLoading.renderCrop(markImage, CGRect(x: cx, y: cy, width: side, height: side)) {\n        let r = try Watermark.match(crop, against: signature)\n        let error = Double(max(abs(r.pixelX - cx), abs(r.pixelY - cy))) / 32\n        Show.line(String(format: \"a half-area crop at (%d, %d) px: %@, score %.3f over %d bits (z %.1f), found at (%d, %d), off by %.2f tiles\",\n                         cx, cy, r.matched ? \"matched\" : \"not matched\", r.score, r.bitsCompared, r.zScore, r.pixelX, r.pixelY, error))\n        let jpegMatch = try Watermark.match(try ImageCodec.recompressed(markImage, as: .jpeg, quality: 0.75), against: signature, options: MatchOptions(phases: [0]))\n        Show.line(String(format: \"the image re-encoded as JPEG q75: %@, score %.3f\", jpegMatch.matched ? \"matched\" : \"not matched\", jpegMatch.score))\n        Show.line(\"(reported, not asserted: whether v1 holds on real crops is `veilgarde watermark accept`'s question)\")\n    }\n\n    // 10. Every checkpoint.\n    Show.step(10, \"verify\", \"\\(checks.all.filter(\\.1).count) of \\(checks.all.count) checkpoints hold\")\n}\n\ndo {\n    try run()\n} catch {\n    print(\"playground: \\(error)\")\n    exit(1)\n}\nexit(checks.passed ? 0 : 1)\n"},{"path":"Playground/run.sh","status":"added","lang":"shell","hunks":[[1,0,1,33]],"header":{"lines":[2,7],"style":"hash","what":[3,4],"pin":[7,7],"in":[5,6],"out":null},"marks":[],"first":1916,"scopes":[],"old":"","new":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only\n# WHAT: Build the playground (release), put MLX's Metal library beside the binary when it is\n#       missing, and run it. Arguments go to the playground: `run.sh clean` removes Playground/.work.\n# IN:   VEILGARDE_METALLIB=rebuild reinstalls mlx.metallib (after a Frigate/MLX update).\n#       VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR as everywhere: else a Frigate checkout beside the repo.\n# PIN:  One MLX workload at a time: never beside training, the parity sweep or GPU tests.\nset -euo pipefail\nHERE=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"${BASH_SOURCE[0]}\")\" && pwd)\"\nREPO_ROOT=\"$(cd \"$HERE/..\" && pwd)\"\n# Frigate, the vendored MLX stack, is taken by path: VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR, else a checkout beside this repo\n# (https://github.com/rao-studios/Frigate). A machine's own settings, kept in a gitignored scripts/lib.sh, come first.\n[ -f \"$REPO_ROOT/scripts/lib.sh\" ] && source \"$REPO_ROOT/scripts/lib.sh\"\nVEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR=\"${VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR:-$REPO_ROOT/../Frigate}\"\nif [ ! -f \"$VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR/Package.swift\" ]; then\n    echo \"veilgarde: no Frigate at $VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR: check it out beside this repo, or set VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR\" >&2\n    exit 69\nfi\nexport VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR=\"$(cd \"$VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR\" && pwd)\"\nexport GIT_LFS_SKIP_SMUDGE=1    # Frigate's LFS fixtures break SwiftPM checkouts otherwise\nif [ \"${1:-}\" = \"clean\" ]; then\n    rm -rf \"$HERE/.work\"\n    echo \"run.sh: removed Playground/.work\" >&2\n    exit 0\nfi\necho \"run.sh: building the playground (release)\" >&2\nswift build --package-path \"$HERE\" -c release --product VeilGardePlayground -q >&2\nbin_dir=\"$(swift build --package-path \"$HERE\" -c release --show-bin-path)\"\nif [ ! -f \"$bin_dir/mlx.metallib\" ] || [ \"${VEILGARDE_METALLIB:-}\" = \"rebuild\" ]; then\n    echo \"run.sh: installing mlx.metallib beside the binary\" >&2\n    \"$VEILGARDE_FRIGATE_DIR/scripts/build-metallib.sh\" release --package \"$HERE\" > /dev/null\nfi\nexec \"$bin_dir/VeilGardePlayground\" \"$@\"\n"}]};
